Hooks for Nightjar's once-a-second video FEC loss report (0x5539, protocol/core/src/fec_report.rs):
every FEC block that completes or is given up calls RL_FEC_BLOCK_FINISHED, and the loss-stats
thread calls RL_LOSS_STATS_TICK beside the periodic ping to a Sunshine host. Both are no-ops
unless the including wrapper (android_rtp_video.c, android_control.c) defines them, so the video
path and the differential tests are unchanged otherwise. Applies after clock-sync.patch.

diff --git a/src/ControlStream.c b/src/ControlStream.c
index 16355a0..64ea71f 100644
--- a/src/ControlStream.c
+++ b/src/ControlStream.c
@@ -1644,6 +1644,11 @@ static void lossStatsThreadFunc(void* context) {
 
                     free(queuedFrameStatus);
                 }
+
+#ifdef RL_LOSS_STATS_TICK
+                // Nightjar's once-a-second FEC loss report goes out with the periodic ping.
+                RL_LOSS_STATS_TICK();
+#endif
             }
 
             // Send the message (and don't expect a response)
